    "Literature (GPLIT), accepted: MPRRS arXiv:1702.01003v5 Theorem 37 (p. 45; Mathematika 65 (2019)), confirmed verbatim at source: for A in a field F of characteristic p with |AA| = M|A| and |A| <= p^(13/23) M^(10/23), E^x(A + alpha) << M^(33/13) |A|^(32/13) for every alpha != 0, where << hides (log |A|)^(18/13); Shkredov arXiv:1802.09066v2 Lemma 43 restates it. It applies to symmetric geometric progressions I in Q with |I| asymp sqrt p after removing the element 1 (M <= 2 + O(1/N)), giving E^x(I - 1) << |I|^(32/13) (log)^(18/13) = p^(16/13+o(1)); primality enters through the size condition (it fails in the F_(r^2) control). The second condition of Lemma 33, not checked in the printed proof, holds or is trivially covered (audit). Consequence: cand:gp-shifted-energy is known at |I|^(32/13), not only |I|^(5/2); the Round 189 admissible-only obstruction weakens from p^(5/4) (one-match 7/4) to p^(16/13) (one-match 45/26); this is a weakening, not a new cap theorem. It does not apply to partial-product graphs; no Round 187 proof used Lemma 33 at height 1. Rounds 186-189 missed the theorem.",
